  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given equations can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>From the given equations we can conclude that the phase difference between the waves is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e. odd multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>. Therefore, destructive interference will happen.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>",
